# Spanish does not agree with itself about "unknown" or about "none detected", so every
# row that says one of them names the row it is read in. The gender follows the row's own
# noun: "la velocidad"/"el ancho de banda" of the memory row is answered in the feminine
# because the label the reader sees is the measurement, while "el modelo", "el contexto",
# "el tamaño" and "los bits" are masculine; "la GPU" is feminine and "los backends"
# masculine.
